# The human hippocampus supports auditory coding and multisensory integration

This dataset contains raw and preprocessed 3T fMRI data from
32 healthy adults which accompany:

  Raccah, O., Agarwal, A., Zhu, Y., & Turk-Browne, N. B. (2026). The human
  hippocampus supports auditory coding and multisensory integration.
  PLOS Biology.

## Participants

32 participants (sub-mm01 through sub-mm32). `participants.tsv` includes
each participant, with an `included` flag and an `exclusion_reason`. Two
participants (sub-mm04, sub-mm12) were excluded from all analyses reported
in the paper for excessive head motion. Their data are included here in
full.

## Task

Each participant completed 9 runs of the task.

Each run's `events.tsv` contains:

  onset       run-relative onset in seconds
  duration    event duration in seconds
  trial_type  trial condition label
  stim_path   partial path of the stimulus file presented on that trial

## Acquisition

Siemens MAGNETOM Prisma 3T (syngo MR XA30), 64-channel head/neck coil.

  T1w   208 x 256 x 256, 1.0 mm isotropic, whole head
  T2w   384 x 384 x 54, 0.438 x 0.438 x 1.8 mm, oblique coronal slab
	perpendicular to the hippocampal long axis.
  BOLD  9 runs, TR = 1.5 s, TE = 32 ms, flip angle = 64 deg,
        multiband factor 6
  fmap  reverse-phase-encode spin-echo EPI (dir-AP and dir-PA)

## Raw data

BIDS layout under `sub-<label>/`:

  anat/   T1w, T2w
  func/   9 BOLD runs, with events.tsv and events.json
  fmap/   dir-AP and dir-PA

## Derivatives

### derivatives/fmriprep/

Preprocessed anatomical and functional data using fMRIPrep
23.2.1. Two output spaces provided:

  T1w                      participant native space
  MNI152NLin2009cAsym      volumetric template space

Also included per participant: preprocessed T2w, brain and ribbon
masks, tissue probability maps and discrete segmentation, cortical
surfaces, the transforms between spaces, preprocessed BOLD, and run-level confound
timeseries.

### derivatives/rois/

ROIs masks used in the paper:

  ASHS/bin_masks_5B_T1/    hippocampal subfield masks in T1 space
  ASHS/bin_masks_5B_T2/    hippocampal subfield masks in T2 space

  harvard-oxford/          Harvard-Oxford atlas:
                             Heschl's Gyrus (includes H1 and H2)
                             Superior Temporal Gyrus, posterior division
                             Lateral Occipital Cortex, inferior division
                             Occipital Pole

  antpost-segs/            anterior and posterior hippocampal divisions:
			     left, right, and combined

